From 032ded0df36aaa82ff25cc41369ff59e7247a57f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:43:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: gas interceptor: panda-timed factory-cruise CANCEL
 safety net (CLU11 only from firmware, after a cluster frame)

If the factory cruise becomes ACTIVE (EMS16 CRUISE_LAMP_S) while openpilot longitudinal is engaged (controls_allowed
and heartbeat), panda builds and sends CLU11 CruiseSwState=4 frames itself, each queued while a cluster CLU11 is being
received (19.8 ms before the cluster's next one): cluster payload, button 4, AliveCnt1 = cluster+1, ParityBit1
recomputed. 4 attempts x 3 frames, >=400 ms apart, >=15 ms rate cap, 12-frame cap, 2 s give-up, stop on lamp off,
abort on a driver SET/RES/pause press, skip MAIN-held / bad-parity frames, none while braking. CLU11 stays out of
the USB TX allowlist; the MAIN lockout (long dropped) is unchanged. Tests: libsafety can_send recorder + 20 tests.

openpilot side: carstate_ext mirrors the episode; factory cruise still on 2.5 s after it rose under engaged long ->
accFaulted (audible 'Cruise Fault' immediate disable), cleared when the factory cruise is off.

integration-3: + TestHyundaiNonSCCFCA11{BrakeTest,RollingTest}Safety::test_test_bit_overrides_timed_factory_cancel
(bits 64 / 64+128 with GAS_INTERCEPTOR, both dialects: 0 self-TX CLU11; positive control pedal-only = 12).
